        {
          "id": "cb07536e-2b60-33d0-a445-bfdd41d7e6ce",
          "content": {
            "id": "cb07536e-2b60-33d0-a445-bfdd41d7e6ce",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "China's Anta Sports exploring bid for Puma, Bloomberg reports",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: Chinese sportswear maker\u00a0Anta is reportedly one of the firms exploring a potential takeover of the German sportswear brand Puma.</p><p>The report from Bloomberg News on Thursday said Anta has been working with an adviser to evaluate a bid, and may team up with a private equity firm if it decides to move forward with an offer.</p><p>The report cited people familiar with the matter.</p><p>Anta Sports declined to comment on the report when contacted by Reuters.</p><p>Shares in Puma rose around 13% in early deals.</p><p>Other potential bidders could include Chinese sportswear group Li Ning.</p><p>And Puma could also attract interest from Japanese sportswear company ASICS.</p><p>Puma's biggest shareholder Artemis, the privately-owned holding company that controls Gucci owner Kering, said it is considering all options for its 29% stake in the sportswear brand.</p><p>Puma recently announced it was cutting 900 corporate jobs as part of a turnaround plan.</p><p>That's after lower demand for its products and a hit from U.S. tariffs on imports impacted its business.</p><p>Puma's market valuation is currently $2.92 billion, according to LSEG data.</p><p>Its share price has halved since the start of this year, as it is losing ground to rivals in an increasingly competitive sportswear market.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: Chinese sportswear maker&nbsp;Anta is reportedly one of the firms exploring a potential takeover of the German sportswear brand Puma.</p><p>The report from Bloomberg News on Thursday said Anta has been working with an adviser to evaluate a bid, and may team up with a private equity firm if it decides to move forward with an offer.</p><p>The report cited people familiar with the matter.</p><p>Anta Sports declined to comment on the report when contacted by Reuters.</p><p>Shares in Puma rose around 13% in early deals.</p><p>Other potential bidders could include Chinese sportswear group Li Ning.</p><p>And Puma could also attract interest from Japanese sportswear company ASICS.</p><p>Puma's biggest shareholder Artemis, the privately-owned holding company that controls Gucci owner Kering, said it is considering all options for its 29% stake in the sportswear brand.</p><p>Puma recently announced it was cutting 900 corporate jobs as part of a turnaround plan.</p><p>That's after lower demand for its products and a hit from U.S. tariffs on imports impacted its business.</p><p>Puma's market valuation is currently $2.92 billion, according to LSEG data.</p><p>Its share price has halved since the start of this year, as it is losing ground to rivals in an increasingly competitive sportswear market.</p></body>",
